&lt;li&gt;Moderate the regional social media and chat groups to increase community followers and increase positive engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore new community-friendly platforms to best facilitate the local community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize online and offline events and meet-ups in your region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, translate, and proofread content that will serve the local community and users well for Binance, focusing on the local market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setup close partnerships with the regional Developer Communities, Universities, Blockchains associations, KOLs, and other web2 and web3 audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy successful online and offline Developers campaigns, such as hackathons, workshops and conferences from ideation to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore new community-friendly platforms to facilitate the expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison between Binance Angels and all departments at Binance to coordinate and support special projects, marketing initiatives and campaigns, community AMAs, communications, among other program tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the recruiting and onboarding of new volunteers for the Binance Angels program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor degree or above, prefer major in marketing&lt;/li&gt;
